1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:05,428
A timer, a converter and a delivery engine will capture ten thousand readings a

2
00:00:05,428 --> 00:00:07,300
second. We'll read every line.

3
00:00:08,300 --> 00:00:16,140
Tick four drivers: adc16, dma, dmamux and tpm. Paste both files and save.

4
00:00:16,640 --> 00:00:24,720
With power off, wire a knob to pin PTE30: outer legs to ground and 3.3 volts.

5
00:00:25,720 --> 00:00:34,600
Lines 82 to 85: board, pins, clock and text. Line 86: the converter.

6
00:00:35,100 --> 00:00:43,502
Line 87 is DMA, and line 88 is its switchboard, the multiplexer. Line 89 is the

7
00:00:43,502 --> 00:00:44,140
timer.

8
00:00:45,140 --> 00:00:48,740
Switch on lines 134 to 155.

9
00:00:49,240 --> 00:00:57,240
Lines 134 to 136: converter zero, setting group zero, and channel 23.

10
00:00:57,740 --> 00:01:04,220
Line 137 is the address of the converter's result box. DMA works with addresses.

11
00:01:04,720 --> 00:01:12,480
Lines 139 to 141: which DMA, channel zero, and its multiplexer.

12
00:01:13,480 --> 00:01:19,800
Lines 143 and 144: 64 samples per buffer, 10,000 per second.

13
00:01:20,300 --> 00:01:25,180
Lines 146 and 147 are buffers A and B.

14
00:01:25,680 --> 00:01:32,080
Line 148 lists them, so code can say buffer zero or buffer one.

15
00:01:32,580 --> 00:01:36,660
Lines 150 and 151 hold DMA's working information.

16
00:01:37,160 --> 00:01:47,784
Line 153: which buffer is filling. Line 154: which is ready, with minus one meaning

17
00:01:47,784 --> 00:01:51,240
none. Line 155 counts them.

18
00:01:52,240 --> 00:01:55,360
Switch on lines 198 to 224.

19
00:01:55,860 --> 00:02:02,577
Line 200 is a wiring switch inside the chip. It says: start a measurement when the

20
00:02:02,577 --> 00:02:06,100
timer overflows, and listen to this choice.

21
00:02:07,100 --> 00:02:16,508
Lines 208 to 212: load defaults, choose 16 bits, pick its clock, turn off continuous

22
00:02:16,508 --> 00:02:18,300
mode, and apply.

23
00:02:18,800 --> 00:02:21,920
Lines 214 to 216 calibrate it.

24
00:02:22,420 --> 00:02:26,420
Lines 218 to 220 choose channel 23.

25
00:02:26,920 --> 00:02:34,092
Line 222: hardware triggers start each reading. Line 223: each finished reading

26
00:02:34,092 --> 00:02:35,000
calls DMA.

27
00:02:35,500 --> 00:02:39,660
With 16 bits, what's the largest number?

28
00:02:40,160 --> 00:02:45,160
Your turn. Pause the video.

29
00:02:45,160 --> 00:02:47,720
65535.

30
00:02:48,720 --> 00:02:52,720
Switch on lines 257 to 267.

31
00:02:53,220 --> 00:02:55,380
Line 260 asks the clock speed.

32
00:02:55,880 --> 00:03:01,640
Lines 262 to 264 choose the timer's clock and set it up.

33
00:03:02,140 --> 00:03:07,820
Line 265 sets the count: clock speed divided by 10,000, minus one.

34
00:03:08,320 --> 00:03:12,480
Line 266 starts it. This function isn't called yet.

35
00:03:13,480 --> 00:03:16,920
Switch on lines 324 to 363.

36
00:03:17,420 --> 00:03:27,148
Lines 326 to 328 describe the job: from the result box, into one buffer, 64 samples,

37
00:03:27,148 --> 00:03:29,580
peripheral to memory.

38
00:03:30,080 --> 00:03:36,640
Line 330 loads the job. Line 331 asks for a doorbell when it's full.

39
00:03:37,140 --> 00:03:40,660
Line 332 allows requests at any time.

40
00:03:41,160 --> 00:03:45,480
Line 333, cycle steal: one sample per request.

41
00:03:45,980 --> 00:03:48,780
Line 334 arms the transfer.

42
00:03:49,780 --> 00:03:56,100
Lines 339 to 341 connect the converter's request to channel zero.

43
00:03:56,600 --> 00:04:01,560
Lines 343 and 344 start DMA and make its handle.

44
00:04:02,060 --> 00:04:09,660
Lines 346 and 347 begin with buffer zero. Line 349 allows the interrupt.

45
00:04:10,660 --> 00:04:13,700
Line 354 notes which buffer just filled.

46
00:04:14,200 --> 00:04:17,160
Line 356 clears the done flag.

47
00:04:17,660 --> 00:04:23,980
Line 358 flips: one minus the index turns zero into one, and one into zero.

48
00:04:24,480 --> 00:04:28,160
Line 359 immediately starts filling the other buffer.

49
00:04:28,660 --> 00:04:34,980
Only then, line 361 marks the full one ready. Line 362 counts it.

50
00:04:35,980 --> 00:04:42,460
Inside main, switch on lines 394 to 399. They wake the board and print the rate.

51
00:04:42,960 --> 00:04:47,520
Switch on lines 422 and 423: the converter and its trigger.

52
00:04:48,020 --> 00:04:51,940
Switch on line 446: DMA.

53
00:04:52,440 --> 00:05:00,120
Switch on line 475. The timer starts last, when everything else is ready.

54
00:05:01,120 --> 00:05:05,280
Switch on lines 512 to 532.

55
00:05:05,780 --> 00:05:09,620
Line 514: is a buffer ready?

56
00:05:10,120 --> 00:05:18,360
Line 516 copies its number. Line 520 marks it taken. Line 521 finds the buffer.

57
00:05:18,860 --> 00:05:21,900
Line 523 prints its number and the count.

58
00:05:22,400 --> 00:05:31,840
Lines 525 to 528 print the first eight samples. Line 530 ends the line.

59
00:05:32,840 --> 00:05:39,652
Build and load. Lines scroll quickly. These numbers are examples. Printing is slow,

60
00:05:39,652 --> 00:05:45,480
so capture numbers may skip. Turn the knob and watch the values follow.

61
00:05:46,480 --> 00:05:51,840
On line 144, try 2000. How long does one buffer take now?

62
00:05:52,340 --> 00:05:57,340
Your turn. Pause the video.

63
00:05:57,340 --> 00:05:58,620
32 milliseconds.

64
00:05:59,120 --> 00:06:04,800
Predict what happens if line 333 says false. Then test it and put it back.

65
00:06:05,300 --> 00:06:10,020
You've read a complete hardware pipeline, line by line. Excellent.

